<<~ ahu slot=`#/bearing`>>
! Layer Composition

Use a layer stack where an artwork is built from independently controlled components. A layer can be valuable only in relation to the full composition. This companion does not add `art-layer()` or require every worktype to use layers.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/roles`>>
!! Name component responsibilities

* `source-bearing` — original material retained for provenance or editing.
* `underpainting` — color, light or support beneath another component.
* `glaze` — a partial color or luminance contribution.
* `registration-plate` — transformed selection from a named source.
* `mask/protection` — spatial inclusion, exclusion or shielding for an operation.
* `typography/attribution` — literal lettering, credits or labels where appropriate.
* `diagnostic/backup` — non-publication comparison and recovery assets.

One component can hold multiple roles. Record whether each should render in the publication export.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/ledger`>>
!! Composition ledger

For each component record source identity, role, bounds, canvas, visibility, order, transforms, masks, pixel alpha, blend mode, layer opacity and expected relation. Track actual transformations rather than implied ones.

```toml
[[component]]
handle = "glaze-A"
role = "glaze"
source = "retained file reference"
canvas = "named base canvas"
transform = "documented"
blend = "actual operation"
opacity = "actual numeric value and scale"
visibility = "publication / diagnostic / hidden"
relation = "changes underlying hue without replacing subjects"
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/process`>>
!! Operate reversibly

1. Preserve original pixels and working source assets when required.
2. Apply transforms and masks to named derivatives; keep coordinate origins and order explicit.
3. Verify each component's contribution in the assembled result. An isolated layer need not appear complete.
4. Distinguish intentional registration shifts from orphan marks or accidental coverage.
5. Inspect technical geometry and intended visual read independently.
6. Preserve an editable master and separately name any flattened publication export.

A composite preview may differ between renderers. When pixel equality matters, test the target renderer rather than assuming identical blend or color-management behavior.

See [[Artifact Contract|ha.ka.ba/lares/api/art-sigils/artifact-contract]] and [[Reception QA|ha.ka.ba/lares/api/art-sigils/reception-qa]].

<<~/ahu>>

